From 898463ba664f3c39c9650160ef50dc508f4d3d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey Payton <joey.payton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:03:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: selective display for plugin-injected turns

A turn a plugin starts with ctx.inject_message is proactive work. Its tool
chrome, streaming and long-running notices would ping the user before its
result is known, and the plugin decides what of the final reply reaches them
(it may hold it). Its thoughts are another matter: users may want to read
along.

plugin_turn_display(event) gives such a turn a display policy:
- defaults: thinking and in-between assistant text shown (delivered quietly
  where the platform supports it: Telegram's "important" mode); tool
  progress, streaming and long-running notices hidden;
- display.plugin_turns in config.yaml overrides the defaults;
- a plugin can narrow it per turn: inject_message(..., display={...}) can hide
  a surface but never show one the user's config hides.
Streaming stays off unless allowed explicitly, since a streamed reply would
reach the chat before the plugin could hold it. Other turns, including
heartbeats and background-process notices, are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
